# fizzreim.lic
# Runs Fizzleworth through the Settlement of Reim (the Icemule Trace dungeon crawl): gets in,
# lets ;treim + Fizzleworth-attack-reim fight, and moves on to the next area when the
# area's rare spawn is dead.
#
#   ;fizzreim            go (see below)
#   ;fizzreim noorb      same, but never spend an orb charge to get in
#   ;fizzreim notask     same, but leave the Base Camp bounty board alone (no GET BOARD / TURN BOARD)
#   ;fizzreim status     print REIM INFO in short, where you are, what it would do; change nothing
#   ;fizzreim turnin     walk to the Base Camp tavern and TURN BOARD (hands in a finished task)
#
# WHAT IT DOES (everything below is from the 11/21 logs unless marked "unverified")
#
#  * Waves. The game spawns one creature at you about every 35 s wherever you stand -- the
#    same in a shop, a tavern, the gate room -- so there is no hunting, you just stand and
#    kill. treim reacts to each spawn line ("An ethereal denizen strides toward you!"), dodges
#    the trap warnings (lean / jump / duck) and starts Fizzleworth-attack-reim, which runs
#    Fizzleworth-attack-ultima until the room is clear.
#  * Rare spawns open the gates. After a few waves in an area "A cold, ethereal mist rolls in,
#    heralding the arrival of the Patrol Leader!" (Village), the Guard Captain (Road); kill it and
#    REIM INFO moves its "flagged for entry for up to the ..." line on one area. This script
#    asks REIM INFO whenever the room goes quiet, and when the flag is past the area you are in
#    it walks to that area's gate room and goes through. (Before the rare is dead the gate says
#    "it radiates with an intense grey flame, rebuking your advance"; the Courtyard's reads
#    "blue flame".) The route comes from Lich's map and treim's room lists:
#      Village  24953 go gate  -> Road 24977         Servant  25110 go door -> Visitor 25120
#      Road     25062 go gate  -> Courtyard 25065    Visitor  25121 go door -> Royal 25130
#      Courtyard 25076 go gate -> Servant 25109      Royal: the Throne Room is 25137
#  * Getting in. A quest that is still running (REIM INFO shows "You have 1 hour and 10 minutes
#    remaining.") is just walked back into -- leaving and re-entering is free for the two real-
#    time hours. A NEW run tries the free daily entry first (Premium: one entry per 22 hours): it
#    goes to the chains and climbs, whether or not REIM INFO's "Time until next premium entry" line
#    could be read. An orb charge is spent only when the free entry is already used -- REIM INFO
#    shows a time on that line, or the chains answer "you will have to wait another ..." (then: GET
#    ORB FROM MY BOOT, RUB MY ORB twice, PUT it back, CLIMB CHAIN confirms "This will use your paid
#    entry"). The orb has 25 charges. Rubbing it clears any quest progress, which is why it is only
#    rubbed when no quest is running. At most ONE new run per ;fizzreim; `noorb` never rubs.
#  * Before a (re-)entry it runs ;Fizzleworth-prep here, then one pass of ;symbolz. ;stand and ;ecleanse run
#    alongside, as in a bigshot hunt (a chain trap drops you for 10 s; ;stand gets you up).
#    `;vars set reim_helpers=stand, ecleanse` changes the list (symbolz and ewaggle are ignored there).
#  * NOTHING SPELLS UP OR BUFFS UNLESS IT IS SAFE: outside Reim, or standing in a vortex room with nothing alive
#    and no attack script running. (Scott 11/27, after an old 20-minute ewaggle ran in the middle of the waves
#    and took his mana from 129 to 8 just before a rare.) The sphere's ewaggle and prep and the symbol pass are
#    watched while they run and killed the moment that stops being true. A ;symbolz found running while it
#    fights is stopped.
#
#  * Full mind. When the mind is full (must rest or saturated) it tries `boost longterm`, then
#    `boost absorb` once the longterm boosts run out, one boost per full mind (the same dance
#    Fizzleworth-duskattack does, but with the replies from the August Duskruin logs: an empty
#    absorb answers "You do not have any Instant Mind Clearers to redeem."). `;vars set
#    reim_boost=off` turns it off.
#  * Quest energy. REIM BOOST HEAL (50 health) when health is under 60% and REIM BOOST MANA (50 mana)
#    when mana is under 40, 250 energy each, while the energy (read from REIM INFO, "Total Quest
#    Energy: N/500") is at least 250. Attack and defense boosts are not used. The attack script's mana
#    refill tries REIM BOOST MANA too, ahead of the sacrifice and Symbol of Mana. `;vars set
#    reim_qboost=off`, `reim_heal_below=N`, `reim_boost_mana_below=N`.
#  * Resting is kept to a minimum, because the quest is a two-hour clock. It only rests (a) after a
#    Reim task has been handed in, if mana is then under 50% (`;vars set reim_turnin_rest=N`), and
#    (b) when it is out of mana, and then only until mana is full:
#      - Tasks: the Base Camp bounty board gives "slay 35 creatures" / "hunt the Emperor". The line
#        "[You have finished your task of culling within Reim!]" sets a flag (that is the 35-kill task's
#        wording; the Emperor task's may differ, so REIM TASK is also polled every 3 minutes when the
#        room is quiet: finished, or an active task turning into something unrecognised, sets the
#        flag too, and the new wording is echoed so it lands in the log). The next time the room is
#        quiet it walks out of Reim, TURN BOARDs, GET BOARDs the next task, and goes straight back in
#        unless mana is under 50%. If TURN BOARD says there is no finished task, no more trips for 20 minutes.
#        A new run also visits the board first. `notask` skips all of it.
#      - Mana: below 30 mana (`;vars set reim_rest_mana=N`) with the room quiet it first runs the
#        attack script's refill (demon mana, sacrifice mana, Symbol of Mana); if mana is still under
#        the floor it walks out and rests.
#      - The rest is at the Thirsty Penguin Inn, Parlour (room 3428, a supernode; the resting_room_id
#        of Picko's skel_troll.yaml; `;vars set reim_rest_room=N` changes it), 47 rooms from the
#        approach. When mana is full it goes back in (a running quest is re-entered free: prep,
#        chains, then the open gates). No rest trip is made with under 12 minutes of quest time left
#        (a finished task is then handed in when the run ends). `;vars set reim_rest=off` = never.
#
# THE SPHERE (the Emperor and Empress). Once REIM INFO says "throne room" they are not waves: they are
# summoned by touching the ethereal sphere in the Vault Entry (25142), through the Throne Room's rhimar door.
# When this script stands in the Throne Room, flagged to it, with the room quiet and 14+ quest minutes left, it
# first goes to the SAFE ROOM below (3 rooms away) and: MANA SPELLUP (free, a few a day), then ;ewaggle for whatever
# that missed, rests there until mana AND health are FULL, then ;Fizzleworth-prep here scrolls (the scroll spell-up --
# which prep skips unless prep_scrollbuff=on, so `scrolls` forces it -- and the rubs) and walks back. Then, with 8+ quest minutes left, health 90%+ and
# mana 85%+ (it refills first, and takes a rest trip to the inn for the mana if there is time and no safe room
# could be used), it does `go door`, then ;Fizzleworth-attack-reim sphere, which touches the sphere and kills the EMPRESS FIRST
# (the berserk one nearly killed Scott on 11/24 by stunning him and shaking the ground until he fell over)
# and then the Emperor. It BAILS OUT under 50% health: stand and `go rhimar door` (REIM CAMP is refused
# inside the castle). Two tries (the second needs 5 more minutes of rest), then it leaves the sphere
# alone. A win (REIM INFO shows the Treasury) takes it through the golden vault door, where it types GET SCRIP
# until "your hand is pushed back by a strange force", and ends the run there: the exit (`go vortex`, twice) and
# TURN BOARD are yours. The same if it finds the Treasury already open while you are in the royal wing.
#   ;vars set reim_sphere=off          never touch it (or run `;fizzreim nosphere`)
#   ;vars set reim_sphere_bail=50      bail out under this health % (default 50)
#   ;vars set reim_sphere_mana=85      mana % wanted before touching (default 85)
#   ;vars set reim_sphere_tries=2      attempts per run (default 2)
#   ;vars set reim_sphere_min_minutes=8
# Anywhere in the Vault Entry or the Treasure Vault that you walk into yourself, it leaves you alone.
#
# SAFE ROOMS (the green squares of the Reim map = the rooms with a vortex; gswiki: "Rooms with a vortex are
# generally safe rooms"). Room ids from Lich's map: Village 24895 Wind Tunnel (the mist room, `go mist` from the arrival
# room 24888), Road 25063 Wind Tunnel (east of the gate room 25062), Courtyard 25094 Barbican, Royal 25141 Narrow Ledge
# (Throne Room 25137 -> 25138 -> 25140 -> `go window`); the Treasure Vault 25143 is the fifth. The servant and visitor
# wings have none. UNVERIFIED: that no wave spawns in them (the wiki says "generally"; nothing in the logs shows Scott
# standing in one). It never types `go vortex` (in 24895 that asks "Are you sure you wish to leave the Settlement of
# Reim?"). It uses them three ways, always a quiet room first and back to the same room afterwards:
#   * before the sphere: mana spellup + ewaggle, rest to FULL mana and health, scrolls and rubs (above);
#   * after a bail-out of the sphere: rest there until health and mana are FULL, then the 5 minutes run out;
#   * out of mana (the 30-mana floor): rest there until mana is full, instead of the walk out to the inn, when the
#     area has one.
# Each of these also puts the Voln symbols up before it walks back.
# Any ;eherbs it starts here gets `--buy=off`: his saved eherbs settings have buy_missing ON, which would withdraw silver
# and walk to the herbalist (out of Reim) for a herb he has run out of.
# If a wave reaches it TWICE in one rest, that room is written off for this run (said in the log) and everything falls
# back to what it did before: the inn trip, waiting. `;vars set reim_saferest=off` = never use them.
#
# HURT. When you are BLEEDING, under 60% health (`;vars set reim_retreat_below=N`), or a head, eye or nerve wound stops
# you casting, this script stops the attack, walks to the area's vortex room (the servant and visitor wings use the
# courtyard's, back through the gates), runs `eherbs --buy=off` there and walks back. (11/27: before this you stood
# eating herbs beside the Shopkeeper, and then bled without going anywhere.) The attack scripts report a casting wound
# in $reim_cant_cast instead of eating on the spot; $reim_retreating keeps them from casting during the retreat. If the
# herbs don't fix it (out of them, say) you STAY in the vortex room, nothing attacks, and it says so every minute until
# you are better. In the pit and the vault nothing retreats. `;vars set reim_retreat=off` = never retreat.
#
# WHAT IT DOES NOT DO. Pitfall traps: the pit creature is fought by treim, then this script CLIMB ROPEs out
# (unverified text). Quest energy (REIM BOOST) is spent only on health and mana. The Emperor task finishes
# with "You have succeeded in your task of killing the Emperor within the Castle of Reim!" (11/24 log); turn
# it in with ;fizzreim turnin.

# SAFETY. Only moves between areas when nothing alive is in the room and the attack script is
# not running. A new run is only started when no quest is running; once per invocation.
# `;kill fizzreim` stops treim, the attack script and the helpers it started.

module FizzReim
  def self.treim_attack;   "fizzleworth-attack-reim.lic"; end
  def self.attack_name;    "fizzleworth-attack-reim"; end
  def self.ultima_name;    "fizzleworth-attack-ultima"; end
  def self.poll;           3;     end   # seconds between steps
  def self.foe_wait;       6;     end   # something alive and no attack script this long: start it (treim waits 2.5 s at most)
  def self.flag_every;     25;    end   # seconds between REIM INFO checks while idle at an area
  def self.report_every;   600;   end   # progress line
  def self.stuck_every;    900;   end   # nag when an area's rare hasn't shown
  def self.approach_room;  24876; end
  def self.tavern_room;    25173; end
  def self.throne_room;    25137; end
  def self.vault_entry;    25142; end
  def self.treasure_vault; 25143; end

  # Thirsty Penguin, Parlour (Icemule Trace), a supernode: the resting_room_id in Picko's skel_troll.yaml
  def self.rest_room
    v = UserVars.reim_rest_room
    v.to_s =~ /\A\s*\d+\s*\z/ ? v.to_i : 3428
  end
  # The scripts a bigshot hunt would have running (hunting_scripts: stand, ecleanse ...). Started when it enters
  # Reim, killed again when it leaves for a rest trip or ends; one you were already running yourself is left
  # alone. `;vars set reim_helpers=stand, ecleanse` to change. symbolz and ewaggle buff, so they are never
  # helpers, whatever the setting says: see "buffing" below.
  def self.helper_list
    v = UserVars.reim_helpers.to_s.strip
    list = v.empty? ? %w[stand ecleanse] : v.split(/[,\s]+/).reject(&:empty?)
    list.reject { |n| %w[symbolz ewaggle].include?(n.downcase) }
  end
  def self.min_trip_minutes; 12; end   # no rest trip with less quest time than this left

  def self.uv_on?(name)
    v = UserVars.send(name)
    return true if v.nil?
    return v if v == true || v == false
    v.to_s !~ /\A\s*(?:0|false|off|no)\s*\z/i
  end

  def self.uv_int(name, default)
    v = UserVars.send(name)
    v.to_s =~ /\A\s*\d+\s*\z/ ? v.to_i : default
  end

  def self.arg?(word)
    (Script.current.vars[1..-1] || []).any? { |a| a.to_s.downcase == word }
  end

  # Room ids per area, from treim's lists (Treim::Geography), index = area number.
  def self.stage_rooms
    @stage_rooms ||= {
      0 => %w[24888 24900 24904 24909 24935 24936 24912 24919 24946 24945 24952 24964 24971 24972 24958 24959 24931 24932 24966 24953 25300 24901 24930 23484 24941 23650].map(&:to_i),
      1 => %w[24977 24978 24989 24990 24991 24994 24995 24996 24998 25003 25004 25020 25019 25021 24997 25022 25029 25030 25035 25042 25047 25046 25043 25041 25048 25049 25050 25051 25052 25053 25054 25056 25057 25058 25059 25064 25055 25060 25061 25062 25063].map(&:to_i),
      2 => %w[25104 25103 25101 25100 25105 25102 25106 25107 25108 25099 25098 25097 25069 25068 25070 25071 25072 25082 25084 25083 25081 25078 25085 25086 25087 25088 25096 25095 25094 25093 25092 25091 25090 25089 25080 25079 25077 25075 25073 25076 25074 25067 25066 25065].map(&:to_i),
      3 => %w[25113 25114 25115 25119 25118 25117 25116 25112 25111 25110 25109].map(&:to_i),
      4 => %w[25125 25124 25123 25129 25128 25127 25126 25122 25121 25120].map(&:to_i),
      5 => %w[25141 25140 25132 25134 25136 25135 25137 25138 25139 25133 25131 25130].map(&:to_i),
    }
  end

  def self.stage_names
    %w[village road courtyard servant visitor royal throne treasury]
  end

  # area => [room to stand in, command through the gate, first room of the next area]
  def self.gates
    {
      0 => [24953, "go gate", 24977],
      1 => [25062, "go gate", 25065],
      2 => [25076, "go gate", 25109],
      3 => [25110, "go door", 25120],
      4 => [25121, "go door", 25130],
    }
  end

  # first room of each area, where a lost character is sent back to
  def self.entry_rooms
    { 0 => 24888, 1 => 24977, 2 => 25065, 3 => 25109, 4 => 25120, 5 => 25130 }
  end

  # --- state -----------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.reset
    instance_variables.each { |v| remove_instance_variable(v) }
    @started       = Time.now.to_f
    @entered       = false          # got into Reim during this run
    @last_flag     = 0.0
    @last_report   = 0.0
    @last_stuck    = Time.now.to_f
    @buffing       = nil            # spell-up scripts running right now (killed if we stop)
    @spellup_at    = 0.0            # when MANA SPELLUP was last cast
    @stage_since   = Time.now.to_f
    @stage         = nil
    @was_busy      = false
    @foe_since     = nil            # when something alive was first seen with no attack script running
    @stuck         = false          # the herbs didn't fix it: staying in the vortex room
    $reim_cant_cast     = false     # set by the attack scripts: a wound stops casting
    $reim_retreating    = false     # on the way to heal, or staying put: the attack script casts nothing
    $reim_retreat_ready = false     # true while this script can do the retreat (in Reim, not the pit or vault)
    @started_here  = []             # helper scripts this run started (killed again at the end)
    @task_done     = false          # the game said a Reim task is finished and not yet handed in
    @energy        = nil            # quest energy at the last REIM INFO (REIM BOOST costs 250 a time)
    @last_qboost   = 0.0
    @task_prev     = nil            # REIM TASK state at the last poll
    @last_task_poll = 0.0
    @task_quiet_until = 0.0
    @trip_blocked_until = 0.0
    @refill_at     = 0.0
    @boosted       = false          # a boost has been used for this full mind
    @no_lte        = false          # out of longterm boosts
    @no_absorb     = false          # out of absorb boosts
    @sphere_tries  = 0              # attempts at the Emperor and Empress this run
    @sphere_block_until = 0.0
    @sphere_refill_at   = 0.0
    @sphere_prep_at     = 0.0           # when the last safe-room spell-up and rest for the sphere finished
    @safe_bad           = {}            # safe room => true once a wave reached it twice in one rest
    @told          = {}
  end

  def self.said_once(key, msg)
    return if @told[key]
    @told[key] = true
    echo msg
  end

  # --- reading the game ----------------------------------------------------------

  def self.title;   XMLData.room_title.to_s; end
  def self.in_reim?; title =~ /Reim (?:Settlement|Castle)|Pitfall Trap/i ? true : false; end
  def self.in_pit?;  title =~ /Pitfall Trap/i ? true : false; end
  def self.at_camp?; title =~ /Reim Base Camp/i ? true : false; end
  def self.room_id;  (Room.current&.id).to_i; end
  def self.vault_room?; [vault_entry, 25143].include?(room_id); end

  # a name for where we stand: the Throne Room (25137) is on treim's royal list but is its own flag step
  def self.area_label(id = room_id)
    return "throne room" if id == throne_room
    return "vault" if [vault_entry, 25143].include?(id)
    s = stage_of(id)
    s ? stage_names[s] : "room #{id}"
  end

  def self.stage_of(id)
    stage_rooms.each { |n, rooms| return n if rooms.include?(id) }
    nil
  end

  def self.flag_index(text)
    case text.to_s
    when /village|township/i       then 0
    when /road|approach/i          then 1
    when /courtyard/i              then 2
    when /servant/i                then 3
    when /visitor/i                then 4
    when /royal/i                  then 5
    when /throne/i                 then 6
    when /treasur|vault/i          then 7
    end
  end

  # {flag:, flag_text:, time_left:, premium_ready:, premium_wait:, kills:, scrip:} or nil
  def self.reim_info
    waitrt?
    lines = Lich::Util.issue_command("reim info", /\S/, /You have slain a total of/,
                                     usexml: false, silent: true, quiet: true, timeout: 8)
    text = Array(lines).join("\n")
    return nil if text.empty?
    flag_text = text[/flagged for entry for up to the ([^.\n]*)/i, 1]
    energy = text[/Total Quest Energy:\s*(\d+)\s*\/\s*\d+/i, 1]
    @energy = energy.to_i if energy          # "Total Quest Energy: 102/500": what REIM BOOST spends
    {
      flag:          flag_index(flag_text),
      flag_text:     flag_text,
      # scoped to the quest-status line: the capture also catches stray lines (11/21 15:34 it took the
      # Lumnis "You have 2,454 points of tripled experience ... remaining" for the quest timer)
      time_left:     text[/Current quest status:\s+You have (\d[^.\n]*?) remaining/i, 1],
      premium_ready: !!(text =~ /Time until next premium entry:[ \t]+You are ready to quest again/i),
      premium_wait:  text[/Time until next premium entry:[ \t]+([^\n]*?)\.?[ \t]*$/i, 1],
      energy:        energy&.to_i,
      kills:         text[/slain a total of (\d+)/i, 1].to_i,
      scrip:         text[/Total Ethereal Scrip for this run:\s*(\d+)/i, 1].to_i,
    }
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "reim_info: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
    nil
  end

  def self.hostiles
    GameObj.targets.select { |t| t && t.status.to_s !~ /dead|gone/ && t.name.to_s !~ /animated|verlok|minor demon|raven/i }
  rescue StandardError
    []
  end

  def self.busy?
    !hostiles.empty? || Script.running?(attack_name)
  end

  # treim only starts the attack script off a creature's arrival line, and loses any line that comes in while it is
  # still reading REIM INFO at start-up. 11/27: the first spawn arrived 1 s after treim started, nothing attacked it,
  # and this script stood waiting for the room to go quiet. So: something alive here and no attack script for
  # foe_wait seconds -> start it from here.
  def self.start_missed_attack
    if $reim_cant_cast || $reim_retreating || hostiles.empty? || Script.running?(attack_name)
      @foe_since = nil
      return
    end
    now = Time.now.to_f
    @foe_since ||= now
    return if now - @foe_since < foe_wait
    @foe_since = nil
    return unless Script.exists?("Fizzleworth-attack-reim")
    echo "something is alive here and nothing is attacking it (treim missed it): starting the attack."
    Script.start("Fizzleworth-attack-reim")
  end

  # --- getting hurt: the retreat to a vortex room ------------------------------------------------

  def self.retreat_below; uv_int(:reim_retreat_below, 60); end   # health % that sends you off to heal

  # head, nerves or eyes at rank 2 or worse, wound or scar: what stops a cast
  def self.cast_wound?
    [Wounds.head, Wounds.nsys, Wounds.leftEye, Wounds.rightEye,
     Scars.head, Scars.nsys, Scars.leftEye, Scars.rightEye].map(&:to_i).max > 1
  end

  # why you should be healing in a vortex room, or nil
  def self.hurt
    why = []
    why << "a wound that stops casting" if $reim_cant_cast
    why << "bleeding" if checkbleeding
    why << "health #{Char.percent_health}%" if Char.percent_health.to_i < retreat_below
    why.empty? ? nil : why.join(", ")
  end

  def self.still_hurt?
    cast_wound? || checkbleeding || Char.percent_health.to_i < retreat_below
  end

  # --buy=off: his saved eherbs settings have buy_missing ON, which would withdraw silver and walk to the herbalist
  # (out of Reim) for a herb he is out of. true when nothing is left that would send you back here.
  def self.heal_up
    Script.run("eherbs", "--buy=off") if Script.exists?("eherbs")
    $reim_cant_cast = false unless cast_wound?
    !still_hurt?
  end

  # Called every step while you're hurt: walk to the area's vortex room (the servant and visitor wings use the
  # courtyard's), heal there, walk back. $reim_retreating keeps the attack script from casting meanwhile. If the herbs
  # don't fix it, stay there with nothing attacking, and say so, until it is fixed.
  def self.retreat(why)
    if @stuck
      if still_hurt?
        say_every(:stuck, 60, "the herbs haven't fixed it (#{why}): staying in #{title} (room #{room_id}) and nothing attacks. Heal or walk out by hand.")
        return
      end
      echo "healed: carrying on."
      @stuck = false
      $reim_cant_cast = false
      $reim_retreating = false
      @last_flag = 0.0
      return
    end
    from = room_id
    room = safe_rooms.values.include?(from) ? from : (safe_rooms[stage_of(from) || @stage || 0] || safe_rooms[2])
    $reim_retreating = true
    [attack_name, ultima_name].each { |n| Script.kill(n) if Script.running?(n) }
    echo "#{why}: to the vortex room #{room} to heal."
    started = Time.now.to_f
    sleep 0.3 while (checkstunned || checkwebbed) && !checkdead && Time.now.to_f - started < 60
    return if checkdead
    waitrt?
    2.times do
      break if room_id == room
      go2(room)
    end
    echo "couldn't reach the vortex room (stopped in #{title}, room #{room_id}): healing here." unless room_id == room
    unless heal_up
      @stuck = true
      return retreat(hurt || why)                 # says so, now and then every minute
    end
    $reim_retreating = false
    echo "healed: back to room #{from}."
    go2(from) unless room_id == from || checkdead
    @last_flag = 0.0
  end

  # --- moving --------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.go2(id)
    Script.run("go2", "#{id} --disable-confirm", { quiet: true })
    room_id == id.to_i
  end

  # Go through a gate/door from the room we are standing in. true if we arrived in `to`'s area.
  def self.pass_gate(cmd, to)
    r = dothistimeout(cmd, 8, /rebuking your advance|You step through|You (?:open|enter|walk|pass)/i).to_s
    if r =~ /rebuking your advance/i
      echo "the gate is still shut (#{r.strip[0, 70]}) -- the rare for this area isn't dead yet."
      return false
    end
    sleep 1.5
    waitrt?
    room_id == to.to_i || stage_of(room_id) == stage_of(to)
  end

  def self.climb_out_of_pit
    return if busy?
    r = dothistimeout("climb rope", 6, /climb|rope|You (?:cannot|can't)|Roundtime/i).to_s
    echo "in the pit trap, no one left to fight -- CLIMB ROPE: #{r.strip[0, 80]}"
    sleep 2
  end

  # --- getting in ------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.hands_free_for_orb?
    GameObj.left_hand.id.nil? || GameObj.right_hand.id.nil?
  end

  # one orb charge: GET ORB, RUB MY ORB (+ the 30 s confirm), PUT it back. true if it took.
  def self.use_orb
    unless hands_free_for_orb?
      echo "both hands are full -- can't take the orb out of the boot. (Empty a hand and run ;fizzreim again.)"
      return false
    end
    r = dothistimeout("get orb from my boot", 5, /You remove|could not find|What were you referring|hands are full|need a free hand/i).to_s
    unless r =~ /You remove/i
      echo "no orb came out of the boot: #{r.strip[0, 90]}"
      return false
    end
    r = dothistimeout("rub my orb", 6, /REPEAT THIS COMMAND|dims slightly|You lift your/i).to_s
    r = dothistimeout("rub my orb", 6, /dims slightly|You lift your|no (?:more )?charges|nothing happens/i).to_s if r =~ /REPEAT THIS COMMAND/i
    ok = r =~ /dims slightly|You lift your/i ? true : false
    fput "put orb in my boot"
    echo(ok ? "orb rubbed (one charge spent)." : "the orb rub didn't take: #{r.strip[0, 90]}")
    ok
  end

  # CLIMB CHAIN up to the village. Handles the "paid entry" confirm. true once inside.
  def self.climb_in
    @climb_refused = false
    16.times do
      return true if stage_of(room_id)          # up the chains and in the village (24888)
      waitrt?
      r = dothistimeout("climb chain", 10,
            /Are you sure you wish to enter Reim|you will have to wait another|tentative step|tentatively begin|sideways leap|dizzying nimbus|climb|Roundtime/i).to_s
      if r =~ /you will have to wait another ([^.]*)/i
        echo "the chains won't take you: #{Regexp.last_match(1)} until the next premium entry, and no paid entry is banked."
        @climb_refused = true
        return false
      end
      sleep 0.5   # the confirm prompt needs nothing but the command sent again; Room.current lags a beat
    end
    !stage_of(room_id).nil?
  end

  # ;Fizzleworth-prep here (the rubs, and the scroll spell-up), then the Voln symbols. All of it is buffing, so it
  # only happens where safe_to_buff? says. scrolls: force the scroll spell-up (prep skips it unless
  # prep_scrollbuff=on; `here scrolls` forces it). true if prep ran to the end.
  def self.prepare(scrolls: false)
    case buff("Fizzleworth-prep", args: scrolls ? "here scrolls" : "here", children: %w[scrollbuff3 qverb ewander])
    when :done
      symbols_up
      true
    when :cut
      rearm
      false
    else
      false
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "prep: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
    false
  end

  # :ready (REIM INFO says "You are ready to quest again!"), :cooldown ("15 hours and 50 minutes") or
  # :unknown (the line is missing or says something else). NB premium_wait also holds the "ready"
  # sentence, so it only counts as a cooldown when it has a time in it.
  def self.premium_state(info)
    return :ready if info[:premium_ready]
    info[:premium_wait].to_s =~ /\d+\s*(?:day|hour|minute|second)/i ? :cooldown : :unknown
  end

  def self.entered!
    @entered = true
    @stage_since = Time.now.to_f
    echo "inside Reim."
    true
  end

  # Is spending an orb charge allowed and possible right now? (noorb, a free hand for the boot)
  def self.orb_ok?
    if arg?("noorb")
      echo "the free daily entry is used up; 'noorb' given -- not spending an orb charge."
      return false
    end
    unless hands_free_for_orb?
      echo "both hands are full -- can't take the orb out of the boot. (Empty a hand and run ;fizzreim again.)"
      return false
    end
    true
  end

  # The orb: one charge from the boot, then the chains (which ask to confirm the paid entry).
  # prepared: ;Fizzleworth-prep here has already run for this entry.
  def self.orb_entry(prepared)
    return false unless orb_ok?
    echo "spending an orb charge."
    go2(approach_room) unless room_id == approach_room
    return false unless room_id == approach_room
    return false unless use_orb
    prepare unless prepared
    climb_in ? entered! : false
  end

  # Whatever state we're in outside the quest: get back to the chains and climb in.
  # info = reim_info. Returns false if it can't or won't.
  #
  # A NEW run tries the free daily entry first: the first time each day just go and climb the chains.
  # The orb is only for when the game refuses ("you will have to wait another ..."), i.e. the one
  # freebie of the day is already spent -- whether or not REIM INFO's premium line could be read.
  def self.enter(info)
    quest_running = !info[:time_left].nil?
    return false if !quest_running && @entered      # the run we started has ended

    if quest_running
      echo "quest still running (#{info[:time_left]} left): going back in."
    else
      state = premium_state(info)
      case state
      when :ready
        echo "no quest running, free daily entry ready: using it."
      when :unknown
        echo "no quest running; REIM INFO doesn't show the free daily entry's timer (#{info[:premium_wait].inspect}): trying the chains first, an orb only if they refuse."
      else
        echo "no quest running, free daily entry already used (#{info[:premium_wait]})."
      end
      if state == :cooldown
        return false unless orb_ok?       # no point walking to the board if the orb can't be used
        board_visit if tasks_on?
        return orb_entry(false)           # no point trying the chains: the game already said wait
      end
      board_visit if tasks_on?
    end

    go2(approach_room) unless room_id == approach_room
    return false unless room_id == approach_room
    prepare
    return entered! if climb_in
    # refused although the quest isn't running: the free entry was already spent after all
    return orb_entry(true) if !quest_running && @climb_refused
    false
  end

  # --- helpers ---------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.start_helper(name)
    return unless Script.exists?(name)
    return if Script.running?(name)
    Script.start(name)
    @started_here << name
  end

  def self.start_treim
    return if Script.running?("treim")
    Script.start("treim", treim_attack)
    @started_here << "treim"
  end

  def self.stop_helpers
    (@started_here || []).each { |n| Script.kill(n) if Script.running?(n) }
    @started_here = []
    Script.kill(attack_name) if Script.running?(attack_name)
  end

  def self.cleanup
    $reim_retreat_ready = false             # without us the attack scripts heal on the spot again
    $reim_cant_cast = false
    $reim_retreating = false
    stop_buffs
    stop_helpers
    DownstreamHook.remove("fizzreim") rescue nil
  end

  # --- full mind: boosts -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.mind_full?
    r = checkmind(7)          # must rest or saturated
    r.nil? ? percentmind.to_i >= 90 : r
  rescue StandardError
    false
  end

  # Replies, from the August Duskruin logs (Warlock, Prime_Fizzleworth):
  #   boost longterm: "[You have deducted 500 experience points from your field experience and have added
  #                    250 experience points to your Long-Term experience pool!]"
  #                   or "You do not have any Long-Term Experience Boosts to redeem."
  #   boost absorb:   "[You have instantly absorbed 1000 experience points!]"
  #                   or "You do not have any Instant Mind Clearers to redeem."
  #   either, in roundtime: "...wait 2 seconds."
  # (Fizzleworth-duskattack's "no boosts left" pattern, /Boosts to redeem/, never matches the absorb
  # failure, so there an empty absorb looks like a success.)
  def self.boost_try(cmd, ok, none)
    3.times do
      waitrt?
      r = dothistimeout(cmd, 5, Regexp.union(ok, none, /\.\.\.wait \d+ seconds?/i)).to_s
      return :ok   if r =~ ok
      return :none if r =~ none
      sleep 1.2
    end
    :unknown
  end

  # `boost longterm` first, then `boost absorb` once those run out, one boost per full mind (as
  # Fizzleworth-duskattack does).
  def self.boost_mind
    return unless uv_on?(:reim_boost)
    unless mind_full?
      @boosted = false
      return
    end
    return if @boosted
    unless @no_lte
      case boost_try("boost longterm", /added \d+ experience points to your Long-Term experience pool/i, /You do not have any Long-Term Experience Boosts to redeem/i)
      when :ok
        @boosted = true
        echo "mind is full: boost longterm used."
        return
      when :none
        @no_lte = true
        echo "no longterm boosts left."
      else
        echo "boost longterm: no answer I know (not trying again for this full mind)."
        @boosted = true
        return
      end
    end
    unless @no_absorb
      case boost_try("boost absorb", /You have instantly absorbed \d+ experience points/i, /You do not have any Instant Mind Clearers to redeem/i)
      when :ok
        @boosted = true
        echo "mind is full: boost absorb used."
        return
      when :none
        @no_absorb = true
        echo "no absorb boosts (instant mind clearers) left."
      else
        echo "boost absorb: no answer I know (not trying again for this full mind)."
      end
    end
    @boosted = true           # nothing to use: don't ask again until the mind clears
  end

  # --- REIM BOOST: quest energy for health and mana -------------------------------------------------
  # `REIM BOOST HEAL` = 50 health, `REIM BOOST MANA` = 50 mana, 250 quest energy each (the pool is 500;
  # kills fill it, about 4-5 a kill, so at the cap the energy is going to waste anyway). ATTACK and
  # DEFENSE (120 s for 250) aren't used. The verb can't be used in roundtime. The replies haven't been
  # seen yet, so success is judged by what came back (+15 or more) and the reply line is echoed.
  #   ;vars set reim_qboost=off          never
  #   ;vars set reim_heal_below=60       heal under this health %
  #   ;vars set reim_boost_mana_below=40 mana boost under this much mana
  def self.quest_boosts(now)
    return unless uv_on?(:reim_qboost)
    return if now - @last_qboost < 8
    return if @energy && @energy < 250
    kind = if (Char.percent_health.to_i rescue 100) < uv_int(:reim_heal_below, 60) then :heal
           elsif checkmana < uv_int(:reim_boost_mana_below, 40) then :mana
           end
    return unless kind
    reim_info if @energy.nil?              # learn the quest energy first (reim_info keeps it)
    return if @energy && @energy < 250
    @last_qboost = now
    qboost(kind)
  end

  def self.qboost(kind)
    read   = -> { kind == :heal ? checkhealth.to_i : checkmana.to_i }
    before = read.call
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    r = dothistimeout("reim boost #{kind}", 4, /energy|restor|health|mana|stamina|boost|cannot|can't|not enough/i).to_s
    sleep 1
    gained = read.call - before
    if gained >= 15
      @qboost_fails = 0
      @energy -= 250 if @energy
      echo "REIM BOOST #{kind.to_s.upcase}: +#{gained} (quest energy left about #{@energy.inspect}): #{r.strip[0, 100]}"
    else
      @qboost_fails = @qboost_fails.to_i + 1
      wait = [60 * 2**(@qboost_fails - 1), 900].min     # a minute, then two, four ... up to 15
      echo "REIM BOOST #{kind.to_s.upcase} gave nothing (#{r.strip[0, 100].inspect}); not trying again for #{wait / 60} min."
      @last_qboost = Time.now.to_f + wait - 8
    end
  end

  # --- tasks and rest trips ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.tasks_on?; !arg?("notask"); end

  # From REIM TASK: {state: :finished/:active/:none/:unknown, line: the status line, finished:, none:}, or nil.
  # Verified wording: "You have finished your task of slaying 35 creatures within Reim.",
  # "You were tasked with: Hunting down the Emperor of Reim.", "You do not currently have a task from the
  # Reim Base Camp." The Emperor task's FINISHED wording is not known yet, so anything that is neither
  # active nor none is :unknown (and the poll treats active -> unknown as "done").
  def self.task_state
    waitrt?
    lines = Lich::Util.issue_command("reim task", /\S/, /New Task Eligibility/, usexml: false, silent: true, quiet: true, timeout: 8)
    lines = Array(lines).map { |l| l.to_s.strip }.reject(&:empty?)
    return nil if lines.empty?
    text  = lines.join("\n")
    state = if text =~ /You have finished your task|You have completed your task/i then :finished
            elsif text =~ /do not currently have a task/i then :none
            elsif text =~ /You (?:were|are) tasked with|still (?:need|have) to slay/i then :active
            else :unknown
            end
    header = /\A(?:REIM TASK|Reim tasks are|Completing tasks|You can (?:get|turn)|Current Task|New Task Eligibility|Total Bounties|\{|ABANDON)/i
    line   = lines.reject { |l| l =~ header }.join(' | ')[0, 160]
    { state: state, line: line, finished: state == :finished, none: state == :none }
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "task_state: #{e.class} #{e.message}"
    nil
  end

  # Every few minutes with the room quiet: REIM TASK again, as a backstop for a completion line the hook
  # doesn't know (the Emperor's). Logs the status line whenever it changes, so the real wording ends up
  # in the log.
  def self.task_poll(now)
    return unless tasks_on?
    return if now - @last_task_poll < 180
    @last_task_poll = now
    ts = task_state
    return unless ts
    if ts[:state] != @task_prev
      echo "REIM TASK is now #{ts[:state]}: #{ts[:line]}"
    end
    if ts[:state] == :finished || (@task_prev == :active && ts[:state] == :unknown)
      @task_done = true unless now < @task_quiet_until
    end
    @task_prev = ts[:state]
  end

  def self.turn_board
    r = dothistimeout("turn board", 6, /Good work|do not have a finished task/i).to_s
    @task_done = false if r =~ /Good work|do not have a finished task/i
    # "no finished task" after we thought there was one: the poll misread something. Don't let it
    # send us out again for a while.
    @task_quiet_until = Time.now.to_f + 20 * 60 if r =~ /do not have a finished task/i
    echo "TURN BOARD: #{r.strip[0, 100]}"
  end

  def self.get_board
    # "You need to wait another 1 hour and 45 minutes before getting a new task." (11/27)
    r = dothistimeout("get board", 6, /You were tasked with|already have a task|need to wait another|eligib|cannot|can't/i).to_s
    echo "GET BOARD: #{r.strip.empty? ? 'no answer' : r.strip[0, 120]}"
  end

  # at the tavern's bounty board: hand in a finished task (or one whose wording we don't know: TURN BOARD
  # is the judge), then take the next one if there is none. force: go and try TURN BOARD whatever
  # REIM TASK said (a task-triggered trip).
  def self.board_visit(force: false)
    ts = task_state
    return unless ts || force
    return unless force || ts[:state] != :active
    go2(tavern_room) unless room_id == tavern_room
    return unless room_id == tavern_room
    turn_board if force || !ts[:none]
    get_board
  end

  # the run is over: hand in a finished task, and nothing else
  def self.hand_in_finished_task
    return unless tasks_on?
    ts = task_state
    return unless ts && ts[:finished]
    go2(tavern_room)
    turn_board if room_id == tavern_room
  end

  def self.minutes_left(text)
    t = text.to_s
    t[/(\d+)\s*hours?/i, 1].to_i * 60 + t[/(\d+)\s*minutes?/i, 1].to_i
  end

  def self.mana_full?; Char.percent_mana >= 99; end
  def self.turnin_rest_below; uv_int(:reim_turnin_rest, 50); end   # after a turn-in, rest only under this mana %
  def self.low_mana?;  checkmana < uv_int(:reim_rest_mana, 30); end

  # Called with the room quiet. true if a trip was made (the caller stops this step).
  def self.trip_check(now)
    return false unless uv_on?(:reim_rest)
    return false if now < @trip_blocked_until
    reason = (:turnin if @task_done && tasks_on?)
    if reason.nil? && low_mana?
      if now - @refill_at >= 60
        @refill_at = now
        Script.run("Fizzleworth-attack-reim", "refill") if Script.exists?("Fizzleworth-attack-reim")
      end
      reason = :mana if low_mana?
    end
    return false unless reason
    info = reim_info
    return false unless info && info[:time_left]
    left = minutes_left(info[:time_left])
    # out of mana: the area's safe room (a vortex room) beats the walk out to the inn
    if reason == :mana && safe_rest(:mana, left)
      return true
    end
    if left < min_trip_minutes
      said_once(:short_trip, "#{left} min of quest time left: not worth a rest trip (#{reason}); a finished task is handed in when the run ends.")
      @trip_blocked_until = now + 300
      return false
    end
    trip(reason, left)
    true
  end

  # out of Reim, optionally the board, then the inn until mana is full. The main loop takes it from
  # there: not in Reim and the quest still running -> walk back, prep, climb, then the open gates.
  def self.trip(reason, left)
    why = { turnin: "a task is finished", sphere_mana: "mana for the Emperor and Empress" }[reason] || "out of mana"
    echo "leaving Reim for a rest trip (#{why}; #{left} min of quest time left)."
    3.times do
      go2(approach_room)
      break unless in_reim?
    end
    if in_reim?
      echo "couldn't walk out of Reim -- no rest trip for 5 minutes."
      @trip_blocked_until = Time.now.to_f + 300
      return
    end
    stop_helpers
    if reason == :turnin && tasks_on?
      board_visit(force: true)
      @task_done = false                  # whatever TURN BOARD said, the trip is the answer
    end
    @trip_blocked_until = Time.now.to_f + 180   # never two trips back to back
    if reason == :turnin && Char.percent_mana >= turnin_rest_below
      echo "mana is #{Char.percent_mana}%: going straight back in (after a turn-in the inn is only for under #{turnin_rest_below}%)."
    elsif mana_full?
      echo "mana is already full: no rest needed."
    else
      rest_at_inn
    end
    @last_flag = 0.0
  end

  # the Thirsty Penguin parlour (a supernode) until mana is full
  def self.rest_at_inn
    room = rest_room
    2.times do
      go2(room)
      break if room_id == room
    end
    echo(room_id == room ? "resting at the inn (room #{room}) until mana is full (now #{Char.percent_mana}%)." :
                           "couldn't reach the inn (room #{room}); resting where I am (#{title}).")
    started = Time.now.to_f
    last_say = started
    until mana_full?
      break if checkdead
      break if Time.now.to_f - started > 25 * 60
      sleep 5
      if Time.now.to_f - last_say >= 60
        last_say = Time.now.to_f
        echo "resting: mana #{Char.percent_mana}%."
      end
    end
    echo "done resting after #{((Time.now.to_f - started) / 60.0).round(1)} min (mana #{Char.percent_mana}%)."
  end

  # --- the safe rooms (the vortex rooms) -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  # area number => room. See the SAFE ROOMS paragraph at the top. The servant and visitor wings (3, 4) have none.
  def self.safe_rooms; { 0 => 24895, 1 => 25063, 2 => 25094, 5 => 25141 }; end

  # MANA SPELLUP: "Instantly cast all of your defensive spells", free, a few uses a day (Scott: 6 for Fizzleworth).
  # Verified from his logs (11/24 19:19): the answer starts "With your advanced understanding of spiritual and elemental
  # mana, you transcend the normal limitations of magic and release upon yourself a flurry of abjurations..." and ends
  # "Cast Roundtime 3 Seconds." The answer once the day's uses are gone has never been seen, so anything else is echoed
  # (it lands in the log) and counts as "not available". true if it was cast.
  def self.mana_spellup
    2.times do
      waitrt?
      waitcastrt?
      r = dothistimeout("mana spellup", 6, /flurry of abjurations|transcend the normal limitations|spellup|no more|none left|unable|cannot|can't|not able|already|used|Wait \d+ sec/i).to_s
      next if r =~ /\AWait \d+ sec/i                  # still in roundtime: once more
      if r =~ /flurry of abjurations|transcend the normal limitations/i
        sleep 1
        waitcastrt?
        echo "MANA SPELLUP cast."
        return true
      end
      echo "MANA SPELLUP did nothing (#{r.strip.empty? ? 'no answer in 6 s' : r.strip[0, 120].inspect}); ewaggle will have to do it all."
      return false
    end
    false
  end

  def self.full_mana?;   checkmana >= maxmana; end
  def self.full_health?; checkhealth >= maxhealth; end

  # --- buffing: only where nothing can reach us -------------------------------------------------------------------
  # Scott 11/27: "we should never be spelling up or buffing unless we are in a safe room". Safe = outside Reim, or
  # in a vortex room with nothing alive there and no attack script running.
  def self.safe_to_buff?
    return false if checkdead
    !in_reim? || (safe_rooms.values.include?(room_id) && !busy?)
  end

  # Run a spell-up script and watch it. A creature shows up, we are moved, or `deadline` passes -> it is killed
  # along with the scripts it runs (`children`). :done = ran to the end, :cut = killed part way, :no = not started.
  def self.buff(name, args: nil, children: [], deadline: nil)
    return :done unless Script.exists?(name)
    return :no unless safe_to_buff?
    @buffing = [name, *children]
    unless Script.running?(name)
      args ? Script.start(name, args) : Script.start(name)
    end
    sleep 0.5
    why = nil
    while Script.running?(name)
      why = if !safe_to_buff? then "not safe to be buffing any more"
            elsif deadline && Time.now.to_f >= deadline then "out of time"
            end
      break if why
      sleep 0.5
    end
    if why
      echo "stopped ;#{name}: #{why}."
      stop_buffs
    end
    @buffing = nil
    why ? :cut : :done
  end

  def self.stop_buffs
    Array(@buffing).each { |n| Script.kill(n) if Script.running?(n) }
    @buffing = nil
  end

  # The Voln symbols, one pass: ;symbolz casts whatever is missing and is then stopped again -- left running, it
  # re-casts them in the middle of a fight.
  def self.symbols_up
    return unless Script.exists?("symbolz") && safe_to_buff?
    @buffing = ["symbolz"]
    Script.start("symbolz") unless Script.running?("symbolz")
    12.times do
      sleep 0.5
      break unless safe_to_buff?
    end
    stop_buffs
  end

  # prep was stopped part way: put away whatever it had out and ready the weapon again
  def self.rearm
    return if checkdead
    waitrt?
    waitcastrt?
    %i[right_hand left_hand].each do |hand|
      item = GameObj.send(hand)
      fput "stow ##{item.id}" if item && item.id && item.name.to_s !~ /scepter/i
    end
    fput "ready weapon" unless %i[right_hand left_hand].any? { |hand| GameObj.send(hand)&.name.to_s =~ /scepter/i }
  end

  # Rest in the safe room of the area we stand in, then walk back to the room we left.
  #   :sphere  MANA SPELLUP (free), then ewaggle for what that missed, rest until mana AND health are FULL, then
  #            ;Fizzleworth-prep here scrolls (the scroll spell-up, which prep normally skips, and the rubs)
  #   :heal    rest until mana and health are full (after a bail-out)
  #   :mana    rest until mana is full
  # Every one of them puts the Voln symbols up before walking back.
  # `left` = quest minutes left: the rest never eats the time the sphere needs (8 min + 5 for the spell-up), or the last 2 minutes.
  # true = it rested and is back; false = nothing was done or the room proved unsafe, so the caller falls back.
  def self.safe_rest(purpose, left)
    return false unless uv_on?(:reim_saferest)
    from = room_id
    room = safe_rooms.values.include?(from) ? from : safe_rooms[stage_of(from)]
    return false if room.nil? || @safe_bad[room]
    budget = purpose == :sphere ? left - uv_int(:reim_sphere_min_minutes, 8) - 5 : [left - 2, 25].min
    return false if budget < 1
    unless room_id == room
      2.times do
        go2(room)
        break if room_id == room
      end
      unless room_id == room
        echo "couldn't reach the safe room #{room} (stopped in #{title}, room #{room_id}); no safe rest."
        go2(from) unless room_id == from
        return false
      end
    end
    echo "safe room #{room} (#{title}): #{purpose == :sphere ? 'spelling up, then resting' : 'resting'} here for up to #{budget} min " \
         "(mana #{Char.percent_mana}%, health #{Char.percent_health}%)."
    t0       = Time.now.to_f
    deadline = t0 + budget * 60
    last_say = t0
    waves    = 0
    was_busy = false
    waggled  = purpose != :sphere
    herbed   = false
    mended   = false
    loop do
      break if checkdead
      now = Time.now.to_f
      if ($reim_cant_cast || checkbleeding) && !mended   # a casting wound or a bleed: heal it before anything else
        mended = true
        heal_up
        next
      end
      if busy?
        waves += 1 unless was_busy
        was_busy = true
        if waves >= 2
          @safe_bad[room] = true
          echo "a wave reached safe room #{room} twice: not safe after all -- not using it again this run."
          break
        end
        start_missed_attack
        sleep 2
        next
      end
      was_busy = false
      unless waggled || !safe_to_buff? || now >= deadline
        if now - @spellup_at > 600                         # a charge a time: not again if ewaggle gets cut off
          @spellup_at = now
          mana_spellup                                     # free, so first: ewaggle then only casts what it missed
        end
        waggled = buff("ewaggle", deadline: deadline) == :done
        next
      end
      hp = Char.percent_health.to_i
      if hp < 90 && !herbed && purpose != :mana && Script.exists?("eherbs")
        herbed = true
        # --buy=off: his saved eherbs settings have buy_missing ON, which would withdraw silver and walk to the
        # herbalist (out of Reim) for a herb he is out of
        Script.run("eherbs", "--buy=off")
        next
      end
      quest_boosts(now)
      break if full_mana? && (purpose == :mana || full_health?)
      break if now >= deadline
      sleep 5
      if now - last_say >= 60
        last_say = now
        echo "resting in the safe room: mana #{Char.percent_mana}%, health #{Char.percent_health}%."
      end
    end
    unless @safe_bad[room] || checkdead
      echo "done resting after #{((Time.now.to_f - t0) / 60.0).round(1)} min (mana #{Char.percent_mana}%, health #{Char.percent_health}%)."
      until !busy? || Time.now.to_f > deadline + 120
        start_missed_attack
        sleep 2
      end
      if purpose == :sphere
        @sphere_prep_at = Time.now.to_f if prepare(scrolls: true)
      else
        symbols_up
      end
    end
    go2(from) unless room_id == from || checkdead
    @last_flag = 0.0
    !@safe_bad[room]
  end

  # --- one step inside Reim ---------------------------------------------------------

  def self.reim_step
    now = Time.now.to_f
    @entered = true          # we have been in Reim during this run: never start a second one
    start_treim
    helper_list.each { |n| start_helper(n) }
    if Script.running?("symbolz")                 # ours is stopped as soon as it has cast; any other buffs mid-fight
      Script.kill("symbolz")
      echo "stopped ;symbolz: nothing buffs outside a safe room."
    end
    boost_mind
    quest_boosts(now)
    $reim_retreat_ready = false

    if in_pit?
      climb_out_of_pit
      return
    end

    # The Vault Entry (behind the Throne Room's rhimar door) and the Treasure Vault are yours: treim itself
    # idles in 25142, and nothing here knows what is wanted in there, so never walk anyone out of them.
    if vault_room?
      said_once(:vault, "in #{title} (room #{room_id}): leaving you alone here, treim idles in this room. `go rhimar door` goes back to the Throne Room; waves are handled again once you are out.")
      return
    end

    # hurt (can't cast, bleeding, low health): the vortex room comes before everything else
    $reim_retreat_ready = uv_on?(:reim_retreat)
    why = hurt
    if @stuck || ($reim_retreat_ready && why)
      retreat(why)
      return
    end

    start_missed_attack
    busy = busy?
    if busy
      @was_busy = true
      return
    end

    # quiet. A fight just ended -> look at the flag now, else every flag_every seconds.
    due = @was_busy || now - @last_flag >= flag_every
    @was_busy = false

    task_poll(now)
    return if trip_check(now)

    return unless due
    @last_flag = now
    info = reim_info
    return unless info
    here  = stage_of(room_id)
    flag  = info[:flag]

    if now - @last_report >= report_every
      @last_report = now
      echo "Reim: #{info[:time_left] || 'no timer'} left, flagged to the #{info[:flag_text]}, #{info[:kills]} kills, #{info[:scrip]} scrip this run; standing in #{area_label}."
    end

    if info[:time_left].nil?
      said_once(:over, "REIM INFO shows no quest time left: time is up. The game lets you stay and fight for about a minute and then ejects you; I keep going until then.")
      return
    end
    return said_once(:noflag, "can't read the 'flagged for entry' line (#{info[:flag_text].inspect}) -- standing still.") if flag.nil?

    if flag >= 7
      echo "REIM INFO: the Treasury is open (#{info[:flag_text]})."
      if here == 5                                  # the royal wing or the Throne Room: the vault is next door
        go2(throne_room) unless room_id == throne_room
        loot_treasury
      end
      echo "stopping here: the exit (`go vortex`, twice, from the vault) and TURN BOARD are yours."
      @done = true
      return
    end

    if here.nil?
      # somewhere off the area lists (the wind tunnel, a stray room): go back to the front of the open area
      target = [flag, 5].min
      echo "not in a known area (#{title}) -- walking back to #{stage_names[target]}."
      go2(entry_rooms[target])
      return
    end

    if @stage != here
      @stage = here
      @stage_since = now
      @last_stuck = now
    end

    advance(here, flag)
    sphere_step(info, now)

    if flag == here && now - @last_stuck >= stuck_every
      @last_stuck = now
      mins = ((now - @stage_since) / 60).round
      echo "#{mins} min in the #{stage_names[here]} and its rare hasn't shown yet -- still fighting waves (the spawns come about every 35 s)."
    end
  end

  def self.advance(here, flag)
    if here <= 4 && flag > here
      room, cmd, nxt = gates[here]
      echo "the #{stage_names[here]} is cleared (flag: #{stage_names[flag]}): to #{room}, #{cmd}."
      go2(room) unless room_id == room
      return unless room_id == room
      return if busy?                       # something spawned on the way
      if pass_gate(cmd, nxt)
        echo "through: now in the #{stage_names[stage_of(room_id) || here + 1]}."
        @stage = nil
        @last_flag = 0.0
      end
    elsif here == 5 && flag >= 6 && room_id != throne_room
      echo "the Throne Room is open: to #{throne_room}."
      go2(throne_room)
      said_once(:throne, "in the Throne Room. treim fights the waves; once health and mana are up I touch the sphere (Vault Entry) and take the Empress first, then the Emperor (`;vars set reim_sphere=off` to leave that to you).")
    end
  end


  # --- the sphere: the Emperor and the Empress -----------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.sphere_on?; uv_on?(:reim_sphere) && !arg?("nosphere"); end

  def self.say_every(key, secs, msg)
    now = Time.now.to_f
    return if now - @told[key].to_f < secs
    @told[key] = now
    echo msg
  end

  # Called from reim_step with the room quiet, REIM INFO fresh.
  def self.sphere_step(info, now)
    return unless sphere_on?
    return unless info[:flag] == 6 && room_id == throne_room && info[:time_left]
    tries = uv_int(:reim_sphere_tries, 2)
    return said_once(:sphere_giveup, "the sphere has had its #{tries} tries this run: leaving the Emperor and Empress to you.") if @sphere_tries >= tries
    return if now < @sphere_block_until
    left = minutes_left(info[:time_left])
    if left < uv_int(:reim_sphere_min_minutes, 8)
      return said_once(:sphere_time, "#{left} min of quest time left: too little for the Emperor and Empress (needs #{uv_int(:reim_sphere_min_minutes, 8)}).")
    end
    # spell up and rest in the safe room first (once per try; the spell-up is good for 10 minutes)
    if uv_on?(:reim_saferest) && now - @sphere_prep_at > 600 && safe_rest(:sphere, left)
      return                                  # back in the Throne Room; the next step re-reads REIM INFO and goes in
    end
    hp = Char.percent_health.to_i
    return say_every(:sphere_hp, 120, "waiting for health (#{hp}%, need 90%) before the sphere.") if hp < 90
    need = uv_int(:reim_sphere_mana, 85)
    if Char.percent_mana < need
      if now - @sphere_refill_at >= 120
        @sphere_refill_at = now
        Script.run("Fizzleworth-attack-reim", "refill") if Script.exists?("Fizzleworth-attack-reim")
      end
      if Char.percent_mana < need
        if uv_on?(:reim_rest) && left >= min_trip_minutes + 15
          return trip(:sphere_mana, left)
        end
        return say_every(:sphere_mana, 180, "mana is #{Char.percent_mana}% (need #{need}%) before the sphere, and there isn't time for a rest trip: waiting.")
      end
    end
    sphere_fight
  end

  def self.sphere_fight
    @sphere_tries += 1
    echo "the sphere, try #{@sphere_tries} of #{uv_int(:reim_sphere_tries, 2)}: door, touch it, Empress first; bailing out under #{uv_int(:reim_sphere_bail, 50)}% health (health #{Char.percent_health}%, mana #{checkmana})."
    r = dothistimeout("go door", 8, /You step through|You must be standing|rebuking|can't go|cannot/i).to_s
    sleep 1
    waitrt?
    unless room_id == vault_entry
      echo "couldn't get through the rhimar door (#{r.strip[0, 80].inspect}); trying again in 5 minutes."
      @sphere_block_until = Time.now.to_f + 300
      return
    end
    $reim_sphere_result = nil
    Script.run(attack_name, "sphere")
    result = $reim_sphere_result || :unknown
    echo "sphere result: #{result} (health #{Char.percent_health}%, mana #{checkmana}, room #{room_id})."
    if result == :won
      sphere_won
      return
    end
    @sphere_block_until = Time.now.to_f + 300
    @last_flag = 0.0
    case result
    when :stuck
      echo "STILL IN THE VAULT ENTRY and couldn't get out in a minute: it's yours."
    when :dead
      echo "dead."
    else
      if room_id == vault_entry && !checkdead
        dothistimeout("go door", 8, /You step through|You must be standing|still stunned/i)   # back out to the waves
        sleep 1
      end
      echo "out of the vault (#{result}); resting before another try: 5 minutes at least, health and mana back up first."
      @sphere_prep_at = 0.0                   # the next try spells up again
      @spellup_at     = 0.0
      i = reim_info
      safe_rest(:heal, minutes_left(i[:time_left])) if i && i[:time_left] && !checkdead
    end
  end

  def self.sphere_won
    echo "the Emperor and the Empress are dead."
    info = reim_info
    if info && info[:flag] && info[:flag] >= 7
      echo "REIM INFO: the Treasury is open (#{info[:flag_text]})."
      loot_treasury
      echo "stopping here: the exit (`go vortex`, twice, from the vault) and TURN BOARD are yours."
      echo "the Emperor task is finished (\";fizzreim turnin\" hands it in at the Base Camp)." if @task_done
      @done = true
    else
      echo "REIM INFO still says: flagged to the #{info && info[:flag_text]}. Not stopping; the sphere is not tried again."
      @sphere_tries = 99
      dothistimeout("go door", 8, /You step through/i) if vault_room? && room_id == vault_entry
    end
  end

  # --- the Treasure Vault ----------------------------------------------------------------

  # Verified 11/27 18:13 (done by hand): through the golden vault door from the Vault Entry, then GET SCRIP paid
  # "You manage to grab 60 ethereal scrip from a pile of ethereal scrip." (then 79, 72) until "As you reach for a
  # pile of ethereal scrip your hand is pushed back by a strange force." `go golden door` is the map's command
  # (before the win the door answers "... rebuking your advance"); a plain `go door` in the Vault Entry once took
  # the rhimar door back to the Throne Room, where it is the right command.
  def self.loot_treasury
    enter_vault
    unless room_id == treasure_vault
      echo "couldn't get into the Treasure Vault (room #{room_id}). By hand: `go golden door` from the Vault Entry, then `get scrip` until you're refused."
      return
    end
    got = 0
    last = ""
    20.times do
      break if checkdead
      waitrt?
      last = dothistimeout("get scrip", 6, /You manage to grab [\d,]+ ethereal scrip|pushed back by a strange force|wait \d+ sec|What were you|Get what|You can't|hands? (?:are|is) full/i).to_s
      if last =~ /grab ([\d,]+) ethereal scrip/i
        got += Regexp.last_match(1).delete(",").to_i
      elsif last !~ /wait \d+ sec/i
        break
      end
      sleep 1
    end
    why = case last
          when /pushed back/i then "that's all it gives"
          when "" then "no answer to `get scrip`"
          else "stopped on #{last.strip[0, 100].inspect}"
          end
    echo "Treasure Vault: grabbed #{got} ethereal scrip (#{why})."
  end

  def self.enter_vault
    if room_id == throne_room
      waitrt?
      dothistimeout("go door", 8, /You step through|You must be standing|rebuking|can't go|cannot/i)
      sleep 1
    end
    3.times do
      break unless room_id == vault_entry && !checkdead
      20.times { break unless checkstunned || checkwebbed; sleep 1 }
      waitrt?
      fput "stand" unless checkstanding
      dothistimeout("go golden door", 8, /You step through|rebuking your advance|You must be standing|still stunned|Where are you|can't go|cannot|wait \d+ sec/i)
      sleep 1
    end
  end

  # --- modes -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

  def self.status
    info = reim_info
    echo "room #{room_id} (#{title}); area: #{stage_of(room_id) || vault_room? ? area_label : '-'}"
    if info
      echo "time left: #{info[:time_left] || 'none (no quest running)'}; flagged to the #{info[:flag_text]} (area #{info[:flag].inspect})"
      echo "free daily entry: #{premium_state(info)} (#{info[:premium_wait].inspect}); #{info[:kills]} kills, #{info[:scrip]} scrip this run, quest energy #{info[:energy].inspect}"
      ts = tasks_on? ? task_state : nil
      echo "safe rooms (vortex): #{uv_on?(:reim_saferest) ? safe_rooms.map { |a, r| "#{stage_names[a]} #{r}" }.join(', ') : 'off'}"
      echo "hurt: #{uv_on?(:reim_retreat) ? "when bleeding, under #{retreat_below}% health or unable to cast, retreat to the vortex room and heal" : 'no retreat (reim_retreat=off)'}"
      echo "task: #{ts ? "#{ts[:state]} (#{ts[:line]})" : (tasks_on? ? '?' : 'ignored (notask)')}; rest: #{uv_on?(:reim_rest) ? "inn #{rest_room} when mana < #{uv_int(:reim_rest_mana, 30)}, or after a turn-in with mana < #{turnin_rest_below}" : 'off'}; boosts: #{uv_on?(:reim_boost) ? 'on' : 'off'}; mind #{percentmind}%, mana #{Char.percent_mana}%"
      s = stage_of(room_id)
      if !in_reim?
        echo(info[:time_left] ? "would: go back in (free)." : (premium_state(info) == :cooldown ? "would: start a new run with one orb charge (the free entry is used)." : "would: start a new run on the free daily entry (an orb only if the chains refuse)."))
      elsif s && info[:flag] && info[:flag] > s && s <= 4
        echo "would: go to room #{gates[s][0]} and #{gates[s][1]}."
      else
        echo "would: stay and fight."
      end
    else
      echo "REIM INFO gave nothing."
    end
  end

  def self.turn_in
    go2(tavern_room)
    turn_board if room_id == tavern_room
  end

  def self.run
    reset
    mode = Script.current.vars[1].to_s.downcase
    return status if mode == "status"
    return turn_in if mode == "turnin"

    before_dying { cleanup }
    DownstreamHook.add("fizzreim", proc { |line|
      @task_done = true if line =~ /You have (?:finished|completed|succeeded in) your task/i
      line
    })
    echo "fizzreim: starting (#{title})."
    if tasks_on?
      ts = task_state
      @task_prev = ts[:state] if ts
      @task_done = true if ts && ts[:finished]
      board_visit if !in_reim? && @task_done      # outside already: hand it in before going in
    end

    loop do
      break if @done
      if checkdead
        sleep 5
        next
      end
      if in_reim?
        reim_step
      else
        $reim_retreat_ready = false
        info = reim_info
        unless info
          sleep poll
          next
        end
        unless enter(info)
          if @entered
            echo "the run has ended (REIM INFO shows no quest time). #{info[:kills]} kills, #{info[:scrip]} scrip."
            hand_in_finished_task
          else
            echo "not entering Reim (the reason is above)."
          end
          break
        end
        start_treim
      end
      sleep poll
    end
    cleanup
  end
end

FizzReim.run
